			"id": "116167940761577335",
			"parentId": "116166526663522627",
			"url": "https://social.lol/@ewie/116167940738029237",
			"author": {
				"name": "evie",
				"url": "https://social.lol/@ewie",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/neighborhood11tydev/cache/accounts/avatars/114/400/187/012/415/238/original/bda25de5ebe9f360.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-03-03T23:55:03.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://thoresson.social/@anders\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>anders</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://neighborhood.11ty.dev/@11ty\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>11ty</span></a></span> will it be possible to offer a version of those pro features without requiring an active subscription (or relying on your hardware)? i don’t use 11ty but i’m overall involved in the ecosystem (since i’m using a js ssg that’s based on 11ty) and i would like for this rising tide to lift all ships. overall feeling unconvinced seeing y’all having people fund a subscription service that they’ll have to pay for afterwards. like the features are cool and i know that base will stay the same, but all this isn’t going to have *no* impact on the ecosystem.</p><p>i guess my point is that i am imagining the best case and the worst case future for this and i don’t feel great thinking the realistic future is that base 11ty doesn’t languish but also this rising tide will only lift the ships of those willing to pay for a subscription.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "116171450113682855",
			"parentId": "116167940761577335",
